From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: v8: ppc: use ISA 2.07 (POWER8) compatible PC load when targeting POWER8

Upstream V8 unconditionally emits `addpcis` (Power ISA 3.0 / POWER9, opcode
0x4F800004 `lnia`) in `MacroAssembler::LoadPC` to load the instruction address
following the PC-load sequence. In V8, `LoadPC` is called in the prologue of
every builtin via `LoadConstantPoolPointerRegister` (3,936 occurrences in
Chromium, 3,995 in Electron), causing an immediate `illegal instruction (4)`
crash on real POWER8 hardware.

On POWER8 (ISA 2.07), PC is obtained via the standard branch-and-link sequence:
  bcl 20, 31, $+4
  mflr dst
  addi dst, dst, 8

This sequence loads CIA + 12 (the address of the instruction immediately
following the sequence) into `dst`, preserving the exact invariant of
`addpcis(dst, 0)` (which loads CIA + 4). `kPcLoadDelta` is adjusted
accordingly from 4 to 12 bytes when `_ARCH_PWR9` is not defined.

When compiling for POWER9 (`_ARCH_PWR9` defined), the single-instruction
`addpcis` sequence and `kPcLoadDelta = 4` remain active.

--- a/v8/src/codegen/ppc/constants-ppc.h
+++ b/v8/src/codegen/ppc/constants-ppc.h
@@ -3065,7 +3065,11 @@ enum BOfield {        // Bits 25-21
 
 constexpr uint8_t kInstrSize = 4;
 constexpr uint8_t kInstrSizeLog2 = 2;
+#if defined(_ARCH_PWR9)
 constexpr uint8_t kPcLoadDelta = 4;
+#else
+constexpr uint8_t kPcLoadDelta = 12;
+#endif
 
 class Instruction {
  public:
--- a/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
+++ b/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
@@ -1144,7 +1144,13 @@ void MacroAssembler::LoadConstantPoolPointerRegisterFromCodeTargetAddress(
 }
 
 void MacroAssembler::LoadPC(Register dst) {
+#if defined(_ARCH_PWR9)
   addpcis(dst, Operand(0));
+#else
+  bc(4, BA, 0, SetLK);
+  mflr(dst);
+  addi(dst, dst, Operand(8));
+#endif
 }
 
 void MacroAssembler::ComputeCodeStartAddress(Register dst) {
